  "description": "Positive/negative fixtures of the macOS catalog rules (wave 2), in the same shape as wave1.json. Each string is `<base>:<relative path>`; base is home (CM_RESOLVE_HOME), temp (CM_RESOLVE_TEMP), downloads (CM_RESOLVE_DOWNLOADS), volume (a selected volume root) or system (CM_RESOLVE_SYSTEM, standing in for `/` below which /Library/Logs and /private/var/log are resolved); a trailing `/` makes a directory. Every fixture is written 30 days old except those in `fresh`. With the overrides pointing at the fixture tree, a rule's candidates must be exactly its positive fixtures; `expect: permission_required` marks a privacy-protected (TCC) app container that the resolver reports instead of reading. Fixtures are not registry evidence: no rule here is registered and every rule stays experimental until it is tested on a real Mac.",
